  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up emergency health assistance to communities in secondary and tertiary displacements in 10 priority counties</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $2 million WHO project is to provide lifesaving emergency health assistance to people living in secondary or tertiary displacement due to conflict and/or floods. To that end, WHO will support 21 static and mobile health clinics with personnel and supplies, equip six health clinics to provide basic emergency obstetric and newborn care, conduct preventative and reactive vaccinations, deploy rapid response teams, and conduct health and education and awareness campaigns, among other activities. In total, WHO will provide lifesaving health services to 262,522 people, including 66,924 women, 71,858 girls and 26,252 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
